                      (    forth6809.asm):05414                                   ; by every S" call, so a second S" call before
                      (    forth6809.asm):05415                                   ; the first string was actually used (e.g.
                      (    forth6809.asm):05416                                   ; registering two REPLACES strings, or a
                      (    forth6809.asm):05417                                   ; SUBSTITUTE template argument) silently
                      (    forth6809.asm):05418                                   ; overwrote the first - confirmed via MAME
                      (    forth6809.asm):05419                                   ; testing and traced precisely earlier this
                      (    forth6809.asm):05420                                   ; session. Retired per user's own follow-up
                      (    forth6809.asm):05421                                   ; testing/design decision: rather than give
                      (    forth6809.asm):05422                                   ; REPLACES its own dedicated copy-on-register
                      (    forth6809.asm):05423                                   ; storage, wrap each string in its own colon
                      (    forth6809.asm):05424                                   ; definition for stable storage instead - but
                      (    forth6809.asm):05425                                   ; that still leaves interpreted S" itself
                      (    forth6809.asm):05426                                   ; capped at SIBUF's 32 characters for any
                      (    forth6809.asm):05427                                   ; single string. Now computes PAD's current
                      (    forth6809.asm):05428                                   ; address fresh via PADW (dynamic - depends
                      (    forth6809.asm):05429                                   ; on CODEHERE, per ANS's own transient-region
                      (    forth6809.asm):05430                                   ; semantics) and writes there instead, giving
                      (    forth6809.asm):05431                                   ; interpreted S" access to PAD's full
                      (    forth6809.asm):05432                                   ; PADMINSIZE-character region (84, comfortably
                      (    forth6809.asm):05433                                   ; above the old 32-character SIBUF limit) -
                      (    forth6809.asm):05434                                   ; SIBUF itself is now unused and retired (see
                      (    forth6809.asm):05435                                   ; the GLOBALS layout notes above).
